WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.450
From zero to a vault our agent maintains, in one evening.

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:07.388
Nine steps, about twenty minutes of typing.

00:00:08.588 --> 00:00:13.328
Obsidian is the storage half, plain text on our own machine.

00:00:13.378 --> 00:00:18.122
Claude Code reads and writes. Links are notes pointing at notes.

00:00:18.672 --> 00:00:25.073
Claude Code can use the filesystem, or M C P. The filesystem needs no setup.

00:00:25.123 --> 00:00:26.958
M C P needs a plugin.

00:00:27.058 --> 00:00:28.648
Start on the filesystem.

00:00:29.198 --> 00:00:36.140
Next, Claude dot M D. We do not type it, we get interviewed. One question at a time.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:41.976
Then scope. The full vault plans. A single project ships.

00:00:42.526 --> 00:00:47.140
For live data, the rule that matters most: keys, not prompts.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:54.342
Last, git. Commit before a big ingest, run the agent, commit after.

00:00:54.392 --> 00:00:55.928
Sync is not backup.

00:00:56.478 --> 00:01:02.508
That's chapter two, setup. Start with page one: Obsidian and your first vault.
